  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 354 AM MDT SUN JUL 5 2026\nAn upper trough moving by to our north will bring westerly flow\naloft Wednesday and Thursday. This will push moisture to the\neast, ending the threat for showers and thunderstorms after\nWednesday. Expect breezy conditions with temperatures cooling a\nfew degrees by Thursday. For Friday into the weekend, a ridge \nover the Four Corners will strengthen and build north while a \ntrough deepens off the coast. Southwest flow will bring \nincreasing temperatures and breezy conditions. Currently, \nensembles slightly favor some influence from the trough, \nmoderating temperatures somewhat. However, if the ridge builds \nfurther west, very hot temperatures would develop across the \narea over the weekend, with highs over 100 degrees across lower \nelevations.",
